{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["supply"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Probe a node now"},"description":"Needs a rent.dev account: sign in when your client offers it, or call rent_signup first. For someone who runs a machine, their own or a VPS rented elsewhere, and wants to sell its compute; to get a machine to use, call rent_create_sandbox instead. Makes the node's next probe due now, and takes a suspended node back to probing. The probe starts within about a minute. Read the outcome with rent_supply_node. A probe already running is refused with `probe_in_progress`. A refusal carries `retryable`, `owner_action_required` and `next`; run `next.command` after `next.after_s` seconds, on a driver machine through npx and with its driver file, as rent_supply_guide says.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"node_id":{"description":"Node id (`n` and 15 characters) from rent_supply_nodes, or from the node kit once a node is claimed.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["node_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"rent_supply_probe_node","outputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ask":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cpu_usd_per_vcpu_hour":{"pattern":"^(?:0|[1-9]\\d*)(?:\\.\\d+)?$","type":"string"},"memory_usd_per_gib_hour":{"pattern":"^(?:0|[1-9]\\d*)(?:\\.\\d+)?$","type":"string"}},"required":["cpu_usd_per_vcpu_hour","memory_usd_per_gib_hour"],"type":"object"},"capacity":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"slots":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["slots"],"type":"object"},"checks":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"code":{"enum":["os_linux","kvm_available","cgroup_v2","docker_version","docker_compose","outbound_443","outbound_7844","disk_free_gib","memory_gib","embed